#######
# Split-horizon DNS service using a root content DNS server
#
# Machine-local location codes, root authority, and various apices.
# 
# See
#   https://jdebp.uk/FGA/dns-private-address-split-horizon.html#WhatToDo
#   https://jdebp.uk/FGA/dns-split-horizon.html
#######

# Pre-define conventional location codes.
# You should use these in your "main" data file, and define any additional location codes (e.g. "ex") as needed.
%lo:127
#%lo:127.0.0.0/8

##
# Private root.
#
# The Makefile constructs various *.data files merged in from other sources.
# This expects the not-necessarily-default assignments of ::2/128 and 127.0.0.0/8 to a loopback interface.
##

.:127.53.0.1:a:::lo
.:0_0_0_0_0_0_0_2:a:::lo

##
# IP address reverse mappings domain apices.
#
# The imported public root delegates arpa. but the arpa. servers have "no such domain" for all subdomains of these.
# Claim these apices for the private root as far as all machine-local clients are concerned.
# Your actual data mapping the addresses in these ranges will be in the "main" data file.
##

